  "id": "Compound::DB01189 - Gene::2567",
  "verbalization": "Desflurane is implicated in the pathogenesis of Gabrg3 through a series of interconnected mechanisms involving anesthetic agents and their binding to the receptor. The evidence suggests that Desflurane, as a cause of Breath Holding Attack, is linked to Isoflurane or Sevoflurane, both of which bind to Gabrg3. This indicates a potential pathway where the anesthetic effect of Desflurane may be mediated through the action of these agents, which in turn interact with Gabrg3. The shared lowest common ancestors—Organofluorine Compound and Anesthetic Agent—suggest a common functional or structural basis for these interactions. The consistent relationship between Desflurane and Gabrg3, despite the varying intermediate agents, points to a general mechanism where anesthetic compounds may influence Gabrg3 through a shared biological pathway. The integration of these findings highlights the role of anesthetic agents in modulating Gabrg3 activity, potentially underpinning the physiological effects observed in the context of Breath Holding Attack.",
